# =============================================================================
#  A_inputEq_VR_Input.in  --  interactive VR (iMD) driver script
#
#  Resumes the shrinking-sphere compaction from the checkpoint written by
#  A_inputE1_VR_Prod.in and hands the dynamics to NanoVer:
#
#      sim = LAMMPSSimulation("A_inputEq_VR_Input.in", frame_interval_steps=5)
#
#  Two things here are deliberate and load-bearing:
#
#  1. There is NO `run` command.  LAMMPSSimulation executes this script once,
#     synchronously, at construction; anything run here would have finished
#     before VR ever saw it.  NanoVer's stepping loop drives the dynamics.
#  2. The NVT thermostat is left fixed at the end.  If it were unfixed, no
#     integrator would remain and the atoms would simply not move.
# =============================================================================

units          real
boundary       p p p
atom_style     full

variable       cutoff        equal 10
variable       charge_cutoff equal 10

# Styles must be declared BEFORE read_data: the checkpoint is a write_data
# file, which embeds its own Coeffs sections and needs the styles to already
# exist.  (This is why there is no `include multiChains.params` here -- the
# coefficients travel inside the checkpoint.)
pair_style     lj/class2/coul/long ${cutoff} ${charge_cutoff}
bond_style     class2
angle_style    class2
dihedral_style class2
improper_style class2
pair_modify    mix sixthpower tail yes
special_bonds  lj/coul 0 0 1

read_data      "A_VR_3_system_step5000.data"
kspace_style   pppm 1e-04

# Restore the clock.  RiMax/RoMax below are functions of `time`, so without
# this the spheres would snap back to their t=0 radii (1 A and 150 A) and the
# pore built during the production run would collapse on the first step.
# Must come before any fix or dump is defined.
#
# This number is coupled to nVRstart in A_inputE1_VR_Prod.in: if you move the
# hand-off point, change it here (and in the read_data filename above) to match.
reset_timestep 5000 time 5000.0

variable    L equal "lx"
variable    X0 equal "xlo"
variable    X equal ${X0}+${L}/2
variable    rate equal 1/100 #A/fs
variable    RiI equal 1.0 #A
variable    RiMax equal "(time<10000)*(v_RiI+0.24*v_rate*time)+(time>=10000)*25.0" #RiF = 25, clamped so the ramp holds once reached

variable    RoI equal 150 #A
variable    RoMax equal "(time<10000)*(v_RoI-1.1*v_rate*time)+(time>=10000)*40.0" #RoF = 40, clamped so the ramp holds once reached

# Confining spheres: a growing inner bubble (the pore nucleus) and a shrinking
# outer shell (compaction).  These use fix indent rather than fix wall/region:
# wall/region aborts LAMMPS outright the instant any atom lands on the wrong
# side of the surface, which an interactive VR pull will eventually cause.
# fix indent applies a bounded harmonic push instead, so a yanked atom is
# simply shoved back and the session carries on.  K=100 reproduces the lj93
# pore geometry to ~0.1 A.
# NB: fix indent's `side` keyword has the inverse sense of region's.
variable    K equal 100.0 #kcal/mol/A^2
fix wallPoreIn  all indent ${K} sphere v_X v_X v_X v_RiMax units box
fix wallPoreOut all indent ${K} sphere v_X v_X v_X v_RoMax side in units box

thermo_style    custom step time v_X v_RiMax v_RoMax temp pe ke etotal press vol density
thermo          50
thermo_modify   norm yes

fix fxnvt all nvt temp 600.0 600.0 100.0

timestep        1.0
